\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The weight operator in the edge basis}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{Order the edges and let #{C} send an edge field to its values in
that order. For the weight multiplication in a
[finite symmetry of a Gaussian background](fdip-004S),
#{CWC^{-1}=\operatorname{diag}(w_e)}. The massive precision
#{Q=\extd_{\mathbb R}^\dagger W\extd_{\mathbb R}+m^2\bbI} therefore has the usual weighted incidence array in
the vertex indicator basis. Loops and parallel labels remain distinct
edge indices in this ordering.}

\p{The same diagonal array is the coordinate form of the
[weighted edge form](fdip-0007). It does not replace the operator #{W}.}
